  "schema": "perch-native-parity-fixture/1",
  "screen": "folder-browser",
  "note": "The folder picker (stock-ui/folder-browser) as the sidebar's Add project dialog holds it: in the dialog panel (the panel fill, 16 px of padding, 30 rem wide, so the browser is 448 px wide) under that dialog's name and host fields, which belong to the `dialog` screen and are not drawn here. The reference is the browser's own box: 480x416, the panel fill with the padding. Props are `FolderBrowserProps`; the host lists a folder through `browse(path?)` and the harness answers from the fixture's `tree` (path to `{parent, entries}`; folders only, `isGitRepo` gives the git badge), with `home` the folder it lists when the host remembers none; `loading` makes it never answer. The folder the browser opens at is the last one used on the host, which it keeps in the browser's localStorage (`perch.dirBrowser.lastPath.<host>`), set by each state's `view.lastPath`. Going into a folder, the filter and the Type path mode are the screen's own state, reached with `steps` (the harness first waits until the listing is drawn, as a person acts only once it is). 'Use this folder' and the keys (`directory.use`: Cmd+Enter and the alternative) call `onUseFolder`, a no-op here. The list is 60 to 260 px high (about ten 25 px rows) and scrolls past that.",
  "dataFrom": "sidebar",
